{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793656526,"nonce":"KXRwzd7j0g4+oNKGHuM2CWXtKBM=","title":"Bind Cloud Sync editor buffers to canonical cloud document histories","message":"Parent: cd54ac37bbbdfea0fa1fcd39288738a7c0b48475ed9ecea3e6cc98ad20c109ed. Prerequisite: 644a5dd shared history/exchange foundation.\n\nWire native/session and desktop editor documents to the owner-authorized cloud history for their published path. Independently seeded disk documents must not be merged into it blindly. Preserve existing private graphs, unsaved edits, selections and per-author undo; fence ambiguous migration, external disk edits and changed lineage without replacing recovery data. Use worker/ash-future handoffs and apply UI updates only on frames. Reuse existing editor CRDT ownership hooks; coordinate with Jam rather than attaching two transaction owners.\n\nOnly published supported text participates. Structural and binary edits remain snapshot operations. Save must integrate the exact shared head before snapshot publication, and reply only after durable cloud acknowledgement; pending local edits remain recoverable offline. Closing tabs releases subscriptions and loaded graphs. Pause/reopen and expired credential recovery must retain local edits. Surface sync readiness/errors without polling idle language servers or blocking the UI.\n\nVerify desktop/browser edits in both directions, offline edits and catch-up, Unicode/deletion/undo, initial text without duplication, saved versus unsaved disk state, close/reopen, process replacement, retired/recreated paths and races with snapshot publish. Requires pushed transport work as well before advertising continuous editor sync.","files":null}]}